/ egyszer haszn\u00e1latos pelenka)<\/em><\/p><p>In some cultures, cloth _______ are still preferred over their disposable counterparts for environmental reasons. <em>(textilpelenka \/ moshat\u00f3 pelenka)<\/em><\/p><p>The invention of the modern _______ revolutionized infant care in the 20th century. <em>(pelenka \/ higi\u00e9niai term\u00e9k (csecsem\u0151knek))<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">pelenka \/ babapelenka \/ textilpelenka<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): sz\u00e1raz \/ tiszta \/ szobatiszta<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 change a _______ = pelenk\u00e1t cser\u00e9l (pl. It&#039;s your turn to change the _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 disposable _______ = eldobhat\u00f3 pelenka (pl. We only use disposable _______ for convenience.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 cloth _______ = textilpelenka (pl. Many parents opt for cloth _______ to save money.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 wet _______ = nedves pelenka (pl. The baby was crying because of a wet _______.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>diaper<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>diaper<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>diaper<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: change a diaper \/ disposable diaper \/ cloth diaper \/ wet diaper<\/span><\/p><p>similar: nappy \/ baby napkin \/ infant brief<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: potty-trained \/ dry \/ clean<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"diaper","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-23","reviewed_on":"2026-06-24","due_at":"2026-06-24T07:54:40+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-06-23T13:04:57+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":f